[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Verification audit remediation criteria

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Independently justified expected behavior
STATEMENT: Compatibility evidence shall identify whether each expected behavior comes from the specification, an independently checked mathematical contract, a pinned implementation observation, or an intentionally reproduced implementation quirk.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Complete result observations
STATEMENT: Quantity differential observations shall jointly retain returned value, numeric representation mapping, scale and unit identity, and distinguish expected failure stage and approved exception mappings. Each component shall have a negative witness demonstrating detection of independent corruption.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Strict comparison and fixture schemas
STATEMENT: Verification tools shall reject malformed or contradictory outcomes, duplicate or missing case identifiers, empty qualification inventories and nonfinite or unapproved tolerances; compare exact integers without binary64 loss; and require explicit per-case tolerances for approximate comparisons.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Assertion-specific closure evidence
STATEMENT: A verified assertion shall resolve its pinned source occurrence, corresponding API surface and executable semantic tests, tested revision, Java provenance, required platform CI evidence and reviewer decision; inventory accounting shall be distinguished from evidence qualification.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Mutation qualification scope and provenance
STATEMENT: Mutation reports shall identify tested source and test revisions, distinguish historical from final-source campaigns, disposition survivors and uncovered mutants, and demonstrate that critical historical semantic faults are detected without counting ignored or uncompiled mutants as verified behavior.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Independent review and honest qualification verdict
STATEMENT: A verification audit shall retain an independent reviewer assessment, findings and dispositions, explicitly identify agent versus human review, and qualify completion claims according to unresolved evidence gaps rather than aggregate test counts.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.
